@{h1}Delegate (function pointer) support

Support for function pointers, but instead of adopting C's famously cryptic 
syntax, I went with something clearer and more beginner-friendly: delegates, 
similar to C#.

Code
// Declare a new delegate (function pointer type) called Callback
delegate int Callback(int, int);

You can use delegates to create variables, store function references, 
and pass them around just like any other value.
